- TypeScript strict mode always
- All API responses: { data, error, meta } envelope
- All dates UTC in database
- All provider tokens AES-256-GCM encrypted before storing
- AWS customer connections use AssumeRole only — never long-lived keys
- All provider logic must implement the correct interface (IGitProvider / ICloudProvider / IIdentityProvider)
- Use provider.factory.ts — never instantiate providers directly in routes
- Cloud scans always run in BullMQ background jobs (when >2s)
- Scanner findings always include: source, severity, resourceType, resourceId, region, remediation
- All file uploads to S3 — never store binary in the database
- All DB queries through Prisma — raw SQL only for pgvector similarity search
- Provider brand colors only on badges — never as primary UI palette
- ENCRYPTION_KEY must be set — throw on startup if missing
